            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for to insure, then the Russian for insurance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: сеть",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сеть (set) — \"a network; the internet; a net\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Я нашёл эту информацию в сети. Ya nashyól étu informátsiyu v setí. I found this information online."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. В сети — online. Социальная сеть (set) — a social network. First of all a fishing net."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сеть (set) is inherited from Proto-Slavic sětĭ \"a net, a snare\" (EtymDB). The internet is a net in the old fisherman’s sense."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
